    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1044">

                <pb facs="0698" n="626" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg626"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Murillo to
                        Mr. Burton</hi>.</head>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bogota</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-21">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 21, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I am advised that, by the death
                    of your great fellow-citizen, Abraham Lincoln, Andrew Johnson has entered upon
                    the discharge of the presidency of the United States of America for a
                    constitutional term.</p>
                <p>From the time the mournful echo of the night of the 14th of April in Washington
                    reached our (community; you have been able to note how deep and painful has been
                    the sensation produced in it, My fellow-citizens have sadly lamented the loss of
                    that high magistrate who, has associated his name with emancipation of four
                    millions of men, and erasing the stigma of an odious institution, a true
                    misfortune in itself; and I, who had the favorable opportunity, almost of
                    intimate association, to appreciate the gifts and to receive proofs of his
                    benevolent character, have united with lively emotion in the just grief of the
                    American people.</p>
            </div>
